 ## 2026-10-20 — Asterinas-first live-file appearance follow-up
 
 The local GPUI consumer now supports explicit `--watch-appearance-profile` with bounded trailing-edge inotify updates, off-foreground parsing, validated native theme replacement/redraw, last-good retention and an independent appearance-error card. Native theme reloads retain imported colors but adopt native typography. The Vue/Tauri source and existing preference owners were not replaced or changed; documentation and the open OS-A6-PERSONAL gate reflect the narrower implemented scope. Final checks passed 201 GPUI Rust and 36 Python tests, build and Clippy; app version/header checks passed (the previous 1,207 frontend result was not rerun). A real nested Niri/Xvfb/lavapipe host window changed dark→light, displayed an invalid-profile warning without exiting and recovered to dark. This is host software rendering, not Asterinas/GPU acceptance. Wallpaper/density/shell-style propagation, automatic app transport, native Tauri runtime and physical-GPU results remain open. Native kernel lifecycle patch 19 and all evidence are recorded in `/workspace/asterinas-gpui/local-prs/PR_NOTES.md`. No credentials, staging, commit, push or remote Actions were used.
+
+
+## 2026-10-20 — Native launcher density bridge
+
+The existing exported density preference now changes nine actual native GPUI launcher query/body/footer semantic spacing consumers: compact uses the existing Vue unit factor 0.9, comfortable uses 1.0 and preserves original default native spacing. Native font/icon sizes, explicit hit-target dimensions and compositor/bar geometry remain unchanged. Live atomic-file/inotify updates, malformed-save retention, recovery and native-theme reload cover density; runtime density survives palette changes but is not written into native theme files. No frontend source, app preference owner, schema or dependency changed. Final GPUI checks passed 205 Rust and 36 Python tests, real binary build and all-target Clippy; app version/header checks passed. Frontend and host-window suites were not rerun in this pass. New native NVIDIA patch20 and its final validation status are recorded in `/workspace/asterinas-gpui/local-prs/PR_NOTES.md`. Physical GPU, RM/GSP/Vulkan, target Wayland/Tauri runtime and full personalization remain open. Only idle reproducible GPUI incremental caches were cleared after compilation to recover critical shared disk space; sources, binaries and evidence were retained. No credentials, staging, commit, push, publication or remote Actions were used.
